WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:05.050
Why do so many of the indigenous cultures
of the colder regions of North America seem

00:00:05.050 --> 00:00:07.050
to share the same legend?

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:12.490
A legend that tells of a monster that lurks
in the forests, bringing cold and death to

00:00:12.490 --> 00:00:14.110
any that meet it.

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:20.170
This creature is an omen of famine, a territorial
beast that preys on human beings.

00:00:20.170 --> 00:00:25.920
Some cultures describe it as an unholy abomination,
a spirit of winter and a warning against the

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:31.820
dangers of selfishness, one that is created
whenever a person resorts to cannibalism in

00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:33.360
order to survive.

00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:39.280
It will gladly devour any man, woman or child
that wanders into its territory, holding a

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:43.399
horrifying and insatiable hunger for human
flesh.

00:00:43.399 --> 00:00:47.129
So how did so many cultures end up with the
same story?

00:00:47.129 --> 00:00:50.170
Could it be because… it’s real?

00:00:50.170 --> 00:00:55.359
Depictions of the beast vary, but it is most
commonly recognized by its tall, skeletal

00:00:55.359 --> 00:01:00.870
form, like a body exhumed from the grave,
even carrying the stench of death and decay

00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:01.989
with it.

00:01:01.989 --> 00:01:07.070
Anyone who encounters one risks being eaten
or transformed into a creature just like.

00:01:07.070 --> 00:01:12.100
The monster’s name means an ‘evil spirit
that devours mankind’ though to even say

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:16.480
the name is taboo, as it’s believed to give
power to the beast.

00:01:16.480 --> 00:01:19.800
Of course, these are all just legends, right?

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:23.970
Stories to warn against the dangers of greed
and selfishness, but otherwise nothing to

00:01:23.970 --> 00:01:24.970
fear.

00:01:24.970 --> 00:01:29.240
There’s no proof that such a beast could
actually be roaming the frozen wastes?

00:01:29.240 --> 00:01:35.490
Many at the SCP Foundation felt the same way,
until they heard about SCP-323, the Wendigo’s

00:01:35.490 --> 00:01:37.030
Skull.

00:01:37.030 --> 00:01:41.590
Kept under lock and key by the Foundation
with around the clock surveillance, SCP-323

00:01:41.590 --> 00:01:46.469
is an anomalous object with ties to the various
Wendigo legends.

00:01:46.469 --> 00:01:53.210
As the object’s moniker suggests, SCP-323
is a skull; not a human skull, mind you, it

00:01:53.210 --> 00:01:56.170
more closely resembles a cervid skull.

00:01:56.170 --> 00:02:00.970
Cervids are a family of mammals that include
most varieties of deer, elk, and other similar

00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:06.299
animals, and this particular cervid skull
sports a tall pair of antlers.

00:02:06.299 --> 00:02:09.520
SCP-323 is definitely not a fresh skull either.

00:02:09.520 --> 00:02:14.550
It shows signs of weathering and a few scars
across the surface, looking as if the bone

00:02:14.550 --> 00:02:18.300
has been bleached and eroded through exposure
to the elements.

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:23.540
The skull is also missing its lower jaw, and
has a sizable hole on the rear underside that

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:26.290
may have been carved using stone tools.

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:32.570
SCP-323 is kept restrained inside an armored
container within a concrete containment cell,

00:02:32.570 --> 00:02:37.030
and personnel are only ever allowed near it
to check the restraints for signs of damage.

00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:42.250
Additionally, any Foundation staff that enter
SCP-323’s cell must be accompanied by an

00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:47.090
armed security officer, and in the event of
a containment breach the entire site is to

00:02:47.090 --> 00:02:48.620
be evacuated.

00:02:48.620 --> 00:02:52.490
Seems like a lot of precautions and safety
measures for an old piece of bone.

00:02:52.490 --> 00:02:57.160
Surely a harmless deer skull could never be
that dangerous, right?

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:58.160
Wrong.

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:02.200
You might be forgiven for thinking that a
skull can’t possibly cause harm.

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:08.630
After all, SCP-323 is just a skull, then whatever
animal it belonged to is dead.

00:03:08.630 --> 00:03:12.160
But this skull is far more than it appears
to be.

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:17.020
Through extensive testing, the SCP Foundation’s
researchers have learned that the skull…

00:03:17.020 --> 00:03:18.580
isn’t dead.

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:21.950
No, this skull is awake and aware.

00:03:21.950 --> 00:03:29.490
It can see, hear and has a sense of touch,
and it can and will react to various stimuli.

00:03:29.490 --> 00:03:35.690
However, this does not necessarily mean that
SCP-323 is alive or even sentient, but it

00:03:35.690 --> 00:03:38.980
definitely appears to have some level of sapience.

00:03:38.980 --> 00:03:43.290
It will target certain members of personnel
that get too close and has attempted multiple

00:03:43.290 --> 00:03:45.010
times to breach containment.

00:03:45.010 --> 00:03:50.880
It also reacts violently to anyone speaking
English or French near it, the only two languages

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:54.340
prohibited inside SCP-323’s cell.

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:59.730
So, while the skull is not technically alive,
it is definitely aware.

00:03:59.730 --> 00:04:03.730
Still, why the need for so many protocols
to keep it contained?

00:04:03.730 --> 00:04:07.100
It’s not as if a skull can just walk off
on its own.

00:04:07.100 --> 00:04:13.250
Of course not, but SCP-323 can move, at least
to a certain degree.

00:04:13.250 --> 00:04:18.870
Often in a reactionary manner, SCP-323 will
vibrate or move on its own.

00:04:18.870 --> 00:04:22.720
For example, turning to watch as personnel
enter its containment cell.

00:04:22.720 --> 00:04:26.870
In most cases, these movements are tiny and
insignificant.

00:04:26.870 --> 00:04:31.870
But other times, the skull lunges, launching
itself at Foundation personnel as it desperately

00:04:31.870 --> 00:04:33.710
tries to get free.

00:04:33.710 --> 00:04:36.410
Now you know why it’s kept restrained.

00:04:36.410 --> 00:04:42.140
So, we have an antlered cervid skull that
can move and has a low level of awareness,

00:04:42.140 --> 00:04:46.390
on their own these would be more than enough
to warrant the Foundation’s interest, but

00:04:46.390 --> 00:04:50.480
the anomalous properties of SCP-323 don’t
stop there.

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:55.580
The skull has an inherent ability to influence
the minds of those around it.

00:04:55.580 --> 00:05:00.820
Anyone spending an hour within a fifteen-meter
radius of SCP-323 is likely to experience

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:04.000
the effects of this influential power.

00:05:04.000 --> 00:05:09.100
This will often result in them exhibiting
uncharacteristic behaviors, thoughts, and

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:14.340
urges, including cannibalistic tendencies
and outbursts of random violence.

00:05:14.340 --> 00:05:19.590
Almost three quarters of people that suffer
the influence of SCP-323 will feel an overwhelming

00:05:19.590 --> 00:05:24.690
compulsion to take the Wendigo’s Skull and
fit their heads into the chiseled hole on

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:25.870
its rear underside.

00:05:25.870 --> 00:05:30.900
If someone attempting this finds that their
head is too big to fit inside the hollow skull,

00:05:30.900 --> 00:05:35.560
there have been cases of individuals trying
to bludgeon their heads on any hard surface

00:05:35.560 --> 00:05:41.380
they can find nearby in an attempt to get
their head down to a more manageable size.

00:05:41.380 --> 00:05:46.820
This will continue until one of three outcomes
occurs: one, the person manages to fit their

00:05:46.820 --> 00:05:47.860
head into the skull.

00:05:47.860 --> 00:05:52.230
Two, they cause themselves so much cranial
damage that they are rendered unconscious.

00:05:52.230 --> 00:05:57.580
Or three, they end up killing themselves through
repeated violent head trauma.

00:05:57.580 --> 00:06:04.030
Of course, if a person actually manages to
fit their head inside SCP-323, then that is

00:06:04.030 --> 00:06:06.230
a different story entirely.

00:06:06.230 --> 00:06:12.980
In these instances, the individual becomes
classified as an instance of SCP-323-1.

00:06:12.980 --> 00:06:17.650
Within ten minutes of wearing the skull, this
person will suffer dramatic changes to their

00:06:17.650 --> 00:06:18.650
body.

00:06:18.650 --> 00:06:23.390
Any and all body fat will be rapidly shed
as their hair also begins to fall out, leaving

00:06:23.390 --> 00:06:26.640
them looking starved and almost skeletal in
appearance.

00:06:26.640 --> 00:06:31.180
Their distal phalanges - those are the bones
at the tip of the fingers - will elongate

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:35.710
and rupture the skin as they become bony,
claw-like appendages.

00:06:35.710 --> 00:06:40.270
The subject will also find that their teeth
have grown abnormally long and sharp, while

00:06:40.270 --> 00:06:44.830
their limbs will blacken as if they were suffering
frostbite symptoms.

00:06:44.830 --> 00:06:50.770
Along with their external transformations,
SCP-323-1 will also get increased strength

00:06:50.770 --> 00:06:52.919
and a heightened resistance to pain.

00:06:52.919 --> 00:06:57.750
They aren’t invulnerable though, and can
still sustain damage and injuries.

00:06:57.750 --> 00:07:03.160
SCP-323-1 will also have a dramatic change
happen to their metabolism, which will occur

00:07:03.160 --> 00:07:06.460
a few minutes into the physical transformation.

00:07:06.460 --> 00:07:11.460
The subject will now need an almost constant
intake of calories, which if they don’t

00:07:11.460 --> 00:07:15.280
receive, will cause them to starve almost
instantly.

00:07:15.280 --> 00:07:21.160
With the transformation process complete,
the new instance of SCP-323-1 has finally

00:07:21.160 --> 00:07:23.060
become the Wendigo.

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:27.730
A terrifying monster with one goal - to feed.

00:07:27.730 --> 00:07:33.300
The SCP-323-1 instance will seek out any human
beings it can find so that it can feed upon

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:34.639
their flesh.

00:07:34.639 --> 00:07:39.260
Those who have witnessed the 323-1 instance
in the midst of a feeding frenzy have described

00:07:39.260 --> 00:07:44.270
the way it violently slaughtered any person
it could find, leaving only a mess of blood

00:07:44.270 --> 00:07:49.770
as it devoured them, their screams mixed in
with the sounds of bones crunching.

00:07:49.770 --> 00:07:53.790
In the times that the creature cannot find
a human to nourish its monstrous appetite,

00:07:53.790 --> 00:07:57.560
it will try to keep itself alive anyway it
can.

00:07:57.560 --> 00:08:02.430
Sometimes it will slow down its movement to
try and conserve energy, other times it will

00:08:02.430 --> 00:08:08.480
ration whatever food is available to it, saving
some of its last meal for a leftover snack.

00:08:08.480 --> 00:08:13.870
And on occasion, the monster will engage in
autocannibalism, a form of cannibalism that

00:08:13.870 --> 00:08:17.199
involves eating parts of itself.

00:08:17.199 --> 00:08:20.480
Humans certainly seem to be its preferred
food source though.

00:08:20.480 --> 00:08:26.400
Even when other sources of meat would be easier
to acquire, SCP-323-1 will zero in on human

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:31.210
beings and do anything it can to make a person
its next meal.

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:38.229
When chasing down its prey, human or otherwise,
SCP-323-1 has been observed uttering phrases

00:08:38.229 --> 00:08:43.590
either spoken in the primary language of whoever
was transformed by the skull, or in the Severn

00:08:43.590 --> 00:08:46.990
Ojibwe, Potawatomi, and Cree languages.

00:08:46.990 --> 00:08:51.630
These are all native languages of the numerous
indigenous cultures that shared legends of

00:08:51.630 --> 00:08:52.820
the Wendigo.

00:08:52.820 --> 00:08:55.140
Where do the phrases come from, though?

00:08:55.140 --> 00:09:00.690
Are they another side effect of SCP-323’s
influence, or do they originate from the skull

00:09:00.690 --> 00:09:01.690
itself?

00:09:01.690 --> 00:09:06.200
The Foundation’s researchers are still trying
to figure that out, and at the moment have

00:09:06.200 --> 00:09:08.880
no clues as to where they come from.

00:09:08.880 --> 00:09:14.900
In one containment breach in 2006, during
which an instance of SCP-323-1 was able to

00:09:14.900 --> 00:09:20.620
kill and devour twelve members of Foundation
personnel, on site surveillance recorded audio

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:22.650
of the creature speaking.

00:09:22.650 --> 00:09:30.450
“Hungry… so hungry” it rasped, while
dragging a body behind it.

00:09:30.450 --> 00:09:33.290
“I… must eat.

00:09:33.290 --> 00:09:36.130
So very hungry.

00:09:36.130 --> 00:09:38.960
Always… always hungry.”

00:09:38.960 --> 00:09:45.810
After this, the sound of a wet cracking noise
was recorded, possibly one of the victim’s

00:09:45.810 --> 00:09:52.020
bones being broken by SCP-323-1 so it could
get to the marrow inside.

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:57.990
The 323-1 instance does at times seem to try
and resist the influence of the wendigo skull.

00:09:57.990 --> 00:10:02.850
Additional recordings captured the creature
saying “Must… not eat.

00:10:02.850 --> 00:10:06.029
I have to eat.

00:10:06.029 --> 00:10:07.620
So hungry.

00:10:07.620 --> 00:10:13.700
So… lonely,” the creature then said, followed
by noises of it eating the body.

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:14.700
“Alone.

00:10:14.700 --> 00:10:15.700
Hungry.

00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:17.700
Should… eat.

00:10:17.700 --> 00:10:18.700
Must.

00:10:18.700 --> 00:10:22.690
Must… eat them all.

00:10:22.690 --> 00:10:27.830
I must eat… to know… warmth.

00:10:27.830 --> 00:10:29.980
So cold!

00:10:29.980 --> 00:10:32.130
Must eat!”

00:10:32.130 --> 00:10:37.380
It seems that even the wendigo has its own
internal struggles, perhaps showing that there

00:10:37.380 --> 00:10:42.200
is still something left of the human who put
on the skull, and that deep down they are

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:45.040
fighting against their cannibalistic impulses.

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:49.760
But where exactly did the Foundation find
SCP-323?

00:10:49.760 --> 00:10:56.400
And is it really the skull of an actual Wendigo,
the famous creature from North American legend?

00:10:56.400 --> 00:11:01.630
In 1997, the SCP Foundation sent a detachment
to Bittern Lake in Saskatchewan, Canada.

00:11:01.630 --> 00:11:06.620
There had been reports of a local community
murdering individuals and leaving their bodies

00:11:06.620 --> 00:11:10.880
in the forest to appease a dangerous creature
residing nearby.

00:11:10.880 --> 00:11:17.240
This creature, as it was later discovered,
was an instance of SCP-323-1.

00:11:17.240 --> 00:11:22.089
Someone had found the skull and succumbed
to its influence, placing it on their head,

00:11:22.089 --> 00:11:24.490
and turning into a monster.

00:11:24.490 --> 00:11:29.810
Ever since, the locals had been killing people
and offering up their dead bodies as sustenance,

00:11:29.810 --> 00:11:35.210
fearful of what would happen if they didn’t
after being brought up with legends of the

00:11:35.210 --> 00:11:36.210
Wendigo.

00:11:36.210 --> 00:11:40.399
SCP Foundation agents were able to capture
the beast, however it died of starvation while

00:11:40.399 --> 00:11:42.700
being transported back to containment.

00:11:42.700 --> 00:11:47.980
They also covered up the recent deaths in
the area by giving the local residents amnestics,

00:11:47.980 --> 00:11:51.410
and creating a cover story about an unidentified
serial killer.

00:11:51.410 --> 00:11:56.050
Prior to this, James Namagoose, a local man
who was involved in the murders was brought

00:11:56.050 --> 00:11:57.390
in for questioning.

00:11:57.390 --> 00:12:01.800
He remained oddly calm when interviewed, but
admitted he had helped move the bodies that

00:12:01.800 --> 00:12:08.230
were being offered up as food for SCP-323-1,
or as he called it, the Wendigo.

00:12:08.230 --> 00:12:12.900
According to James, a local story among the
Cree people told of men who had once tried

00:12:12.900 --> 00:12:17.670
to control a Wendigo, and perhaps even tame
it through offerings of food.

00:12:17.670 --> 00:12:22.380
Whether or not James and his fellow locals
had the same intention, their primary concern

00:12:22.380 --> 00:12:24.310
was keeping themselves safe.

00:12:24.310 --> 00:12:28.920
He described first encountering the creature:
“A warped man walked out of the woods, killed

00:12:28.920 --> 00:12:30.740
our friends right in front of us.

00:12:30.740 --> 00:12:35.060
Sometimes it would stare more than it would
make to kill, try to talk to you.

00:12:35.060 --> 00:12:38.050
It whispered at me, ‘pe misto’, ‘come
and eat’.

00:12:38.050 --> 00:12:39.890
It made me cold in my bones.”

00:12:39.890 --> 00:12:44.230
As the interview continued, James claimed
he had felt like he understood this ‘warped

00:12:44.230 --> 00:12:45.230
man’.

00:12:45.230 --> 00:12:48.680
He described feeling like the Wendigo was
encouraging him to kill, that the creature

00:12:48.680 --> 00:12:51.770
would help him pass when his own time came.

00:12:51.770 --> 00:12:55.770
James told the Foundation doctor questioning
him that he had heard the creature in his

00:12:55.770 --> 00:12:59.330
mind, and had felt it watching him almost
constantly.

00:12:59.330 --> 00:13:03.380
Mr Namagoose stated that he’d hoped, in
killing people as offerings to the Wendigo,

00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:05.850
that his own family would be spared.

00:13:05.850 --> 00:13:10.670
Like the other locals, James Namagoose was
given amnestics to forget all about the creature

00:13:10.670 --> 00:13:13.160
and the murders he’d played a part in committing.

00:13:13.160 --> 00:13:17.510
So far, none of the Foundation’s staff have
experienced any similar behavioral effects

00:13:17.510 --> 00:13:19.750
to those James described.

00:13:19.750 --> 00:13:26.370
Those who work closely with SCP-323 or have
witnessed an instance of SCP-323-1, have felt

00:13:26.370 --> 00:13:31.250
the creature communicating with them, or urging
them to kill on its behalf.

00:13:31.250 --> 00:13:37.690
Ultimately, who’s to say if SCP-323 is the
skull of a Wendigo like those from the legends?

00:13:37.690 --> 00:13:42.760
It certainly seems like it is, but with no
way to tell exactly how old the skull is,

00:13:42.760 --> 00:13:47.810
perhaps it’s actually the reverse and it
was the Wendigo legend that spawned from instances

00:13:47.810 --> 00:13:53.630
of SCP-323-1 that were first encountered by
indigenous North American cultures hundreds

00:13:53.630 --> 00:13:55.279
of years ago.

00:13:55.279 --> 00:14:01.110
One thing is for certain, if you ever come
across a skull with tall antlers, you should

00:14:01.110 --> 00:14:03.240
try to resist putting it on.

00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:07.430
Otherwise, you might not be feeling like yourself
for much longer.

00:14:07.430 --> 00:14:13.279
Now go check out “SCP-3166 - Monster Garfield
Attack (Gorefield)” and “SCP-2317 - The

00:14:13.279 --> 00:14:20.670
Devourer of Worlds / A Door to Another World”
for more monstrous SCPs that’ll haunt your

00:14:20.670 --> 00:14:21.290
dreams!

